# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session secret — authentication (required in production)
#
# The HMAC key used to sign session tokens. Purbo has no identity provider:
# users authenticate by signing a server-issued nonce with an Ed25519 key
# derived from their recovery phrase, and this secret only protects the
# short-lived token issued afterwards.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 48
#
# Rotating it signs everyone out; it can never decrypt anything.
# In development it may be left empty — an ephemeral per-process secret is
# used instead, so sessions simply do not survive a restart.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage — encrypted vault blobs (required in production)
#
# Any Upstash-compatible Redis REST endpoint. On Vercel, adding a Redis or
# Upstash integration populates KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN, which
# are read as fallbacks, so either pair works.
#
# This store only ever holds ciphertext: the wrapped root key, AES-256-GCM
# sealed entries, and sealed passkey records. Nothing here is readable without
# the user's passphrase, recovery phrase, or a registered authenticator.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
